course: dictionary
lesson: 3311
title: Words from church and faith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about special things, like religion, and you may not know them yet. Context helps you work out what they mean. Look at the words around the new word and ask: what would fit here?
explain: «Holy Communion, also called the Eucharist, Mass or the Lord's Supper, shares bread and wine.» The words «also called» are a clue. They tell you that the Eucharist is another name for Holy Communion, so both names mean the same service.
explain: The sentence also says what happens: bread and wine are shared. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «the Eucharist» means the church service where bread and wine are shared, the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Different churches understand the Eucharist in different ways. Some believe the bread and wine truly become the body and blood of Christ, and others see it as a holy way of remembering him. When a text shows different views, read carefully and do not guess one meaning for everyone.
fact: The Eucharist is a Christian church service where bread and wine are blessed and shared.
fact: The Eucharist remembers Jesus's Last Supper with his friends.
fact: The Eucharist is also called Holy Communion, the Mass or the Lord's Supper.
fact: The word «eucharist» can also mean the bread and wine themselves.
fact: Many Christians believe the bread and wine become, or show, the body and blood of Christ, but churches understand this differently.
exercise: «Holy Communion, also called the Eucharist, Mass or the Lord's Supper, shares bread and wine.» What do the words «also called» tell you? | It shows that the bread is a gift | It means the service has been cancelled | It says the bread has gone stale | *It gives another name for the same thing
exercise: Christians celebrate the Eucharist because Jesus said «Do this in remembrance of me». What does remembrance mean? | A large kitchen where food is cooked | Forgetting something on purpose | A kind of music played in church | *Keeping someone in mind so you do not forget them
exercise: Which is another name for the Eucharist? | Harvest festival | *The Lord's Supper | Bible class | Easter egg hunt
test: In the Eucharist, which things are shared? | Milk and cake | *Bread and wine | Water and biscuits | Apples and honey
test: The Eucharist remembers which meal of Jesus? | *The Last Supper | A birthday party | A harvest dinner | A school picnic
exam: Which statement about the Eucharist is correct? | It means a loud prayer shouted outside | It is a type of cake sold in shops | *Christians celebrate it to remember Jesus, and different churches understand it differently | It only happens on birthdays
